1
00:00:00,375 --> 00:00:01,334
You're saying 

2
00:00:01,501 --> 00:00:04,838
that you have a 
salary of two million?

3
00:00:05,422 --> 00:00:07,841
Two... two million, 
but please.

4
00:00:08,174 --> 00:00:09,426
A loser like you 

5
00:00:09,426 --> 00:00:12,303
couldn't make that kind of money like ten lifetimes.

6
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:12,846
No.

7
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:14,556
Oliver, 

8
00:00:14,764 --> 00:00:17,267
my son is trying to help your son get a decent job.

9
00:00:17,559 --> 00:00:19,185
And he throws out
a figure like that.

10
00:00:19,185 --> 00:00:21,187
He clearly doesn't 
want the job.

11
00:00:22,147 --> 00:00:23,064
He didn't mean it.

12
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:25,734
It was a joke.

13
00:00:26,985 --> 00:00:27,610
Allen, 

14
00:00:28,111 --> 00:00:30,488
if you could get Ted a position with the Knights, 

15
00:00:31,281 --> 00:00:33,408
I would make sure 
I thank you properly.

16
00:00:34,284 --> 00:00:34,909
Oh, 

17
00:00:34,951 --> 00:00:35,744
please. 

18
00:00:36,244 --> 00:00:38,830
What could a broke 
man like you give me

19
00:00:39,164 --> 00:00:40,373
that is worth my time?

20
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,083
Dad, hey.

21
00:00:42,709 --> 00:00:45,128
You do not need to beg them for anything, okay? 

22
00:00:46,379 --> 00:00:47,922
I already work 
for the Knights.

23
00:00:49,132 --> 00:00:49,716
What?

24
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,844
You work for the Knights?
